              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %p
            Hopf algebroids have a base and a total algebra (and some other data). There are 3 levels of generality: commutative Hopf algebras (classical case, both base and the total space are commutative), Hopf algebras with commutative base (studied from late 1980s: Maltsionitis, later Connes’ school etc) and genuinely noncommutative case for which see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebroid"} Hopf algebroid
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bialgebroid"} bialgebroid
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Just as for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            and their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebras"} Hopf algebras
            %em two
            ways to assign a
            %strong Hopf algebroid over a commutative base algebra
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroids"}> commutative Hopf algebroids
                ) with
                = succeed ":" do
                  %strong commutative but non-co-commutative total algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_1)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_0)
                and regard the operation induced by the partially defined
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
                as an in general non-co-commutative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
                structure on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_1)
                over
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_0)
            %li
              %p
                with
                = succeed ":" do
                  %strong non-commutative but co-commutative total algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebra"} groupoid convolution algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi conv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{conv}(\mathcal{G})
                and regard it as a co-commutative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
                over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_0)
          %p
            Given an internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Aff
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff_k
            of affine algebraic
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a field, the
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+sections"} global sections
            over the scheme of objects and the scheme of morphisms have an additional structure of a commutative Hopf algebroid. In fact this is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+equivalence"} antiequivalence of categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brave+new+algebra"} brave new algebra
            (the work of John Rognes).
          %h2#higher_groupoid_convolution_algebras_and_nvector_spacesnmodules Higher groupoid convolution algebras and n-vector spaces/n-modules
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            We discuss here a natural generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebras"} groupoid convolution algebras
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebras
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoid"} higher groupoids
          %p
            There may be several sensible such generalizations. The one discussed now follows the principle of iterated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            and naturally matches to the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-modules"} n-modules
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-vector+spaces"}> n-vector spaces
            ) as they appear in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} extended prequantum field theory
          %p
            In order to disentangle conceptual from technical aspects, we first discuss
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} geometrically discrete higher groupoids
          %p The consideration are based on the following
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-module"} 2-module
              we may think of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Alg_b
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodules"} bimodules
              between them as a model for the 2-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Mod"} 2Mod
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-modules"} 2-modules
              that admit a 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-vector+spaces"}> 2-vector spaces
              ). Hence the groupoid convolution algebra constructiuon is a 2-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \;\colon\; Grpd \to 2 Mod
                    \\,.
            %p
              There is then the following systematic refinement of this to higher groupoids and higher algebra: by the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-module"} n-module
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Mod"} 2Mod
              and maps between them are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
              objects in there. An algebra object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Alg_b
              is equivalently a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquialgebra"} sesquialgebra
            %p
              Special cases of this are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bialgebras"} bialgebras
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebras"} Hopf algebras
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DoubleGroupoid2AlgebraOfDeloopingOfFiniteGroup"}
              below.
          %p
            This iterated internalization on the codomain of the groupoid convolution algebra functor has a natural analog on its domain: a 2-groupoid we may present by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+groupoid"} double groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object in an (∞,1)-category
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            which is 3-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} coskeletal
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
              hence a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+groupoid"} double groupoid
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              to the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet \in Grpd^{\Delta^{op}}
              yields:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  groupoid convolution algebras
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_0)
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_1)
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-bimodule," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mrow
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi 𝒢
                                %mrow
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_1) \otimes_{C(\mathcal{G}_{0,1})} C(\mathcal{G}_1)-C(\mathcal{G}_{0})
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  functor
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 1
                          %munder
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi 𝒢
                                %mn 0
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_1 \colon \mathcal{G}_1 \underset{\mathcal{G}_0}{\times} \mathcal{G}_1 \to \mathcal{G}_1
            %p
              Under the 2-functoriality of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
              satisfied by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              make this bimodule exhibi a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquialgebra"} sesquialgebra
              structure over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\mathcal{G}_{0,1})
            %p
              This sesquialgebra we call the the
              %strong double groupoid convolution 2-algebra
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
            %p
              (Here we make invariant sense of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              by evaluating on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy fibrant
              representative.)
          #DoubleGroupoid2AlgebraOfDeloopingOfFiniteGroup.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
