          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#BakerLazarev01"}> Baker-Lazarev 01
            ), further discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#BakerJeanneret02"}> Baker-Jeanneret 02
            ) (there expressed in terms of the presentation by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
            in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel"} Ravenel, chapter 2, prop. 2.2.8
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroids"} commutative Hopf algebroids
            where the base is kept tcommutative while having the total algebra noncommutative, and the image of source and target maps are required to commute mutually is due Maltsiniotis; he also generalized this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-Hopf+algebra"} quasi-Hopf
            version:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+Maltsiniotis"}> Georges Maltsiniotis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groupoïdes quantiques
              %p
                Rendus Acad. Sci. Paris
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 314
                %a{:href => "http://people.math.jussieu.fr/~maltsin/ps/GRN-1.PS"} ps
            %li
              G. Maltsiniotis,
              %em Quasi-groupoïdes quantiques
              (travail en commun avec A. Bruguières), C.R. Acad. Sci. Paris
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 319
              %a{:href => "http://people.math.jussieu.fr/~maltsin/ps/N-QSBIG.PS"} ps
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laiachi+El+Kaoutit"}> Laiachi El Kaoutit
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Representative functions on discrete groupoids and duality with Hopf algebroids
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3109"} arxiv/1311.3109
          %p
            For the relation to
